WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:11.411 line:0%
MARY MILLER:
BEFORE I MOVED HERE I'VE

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:14.780 line:0%
NEVER USED A CHAINSAW.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.318 line:0%
I COULDN'T EVEN LIFT THE
MAUL FOR SPLITTING ROUNDS.

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:19.585 line:0%
CURLY: ALL RIGHT.

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:21.253 line:0%
MARY MILLER:
THIS IS THE SPOT.

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:23.656 line:0%
CURLY: YEAH, THERE IS
ONE RIGHT UP HERE THAT

00:00:23.757 --> 00:00:25.825 line:0%
I HAD PICKED OUT
FOR YA THERE.

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:29.528 line:0%
MARY MILLER: THERE'S A LOT
OF CEDARS UP IN THERE.

00:00:29.628 --> 00:00:31.531 line:0%
CURLY: TREE FELLING IS
A VERY DANGEROUS,

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:36.869 line:0%
DANGEROUS OCCUPATION.

00:00:36.969 --> 00:00:38.938 line:0%
YOU GOT TO REMEMBER THAT SAW
IS NOT YOUR FRIEND.

00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:42.375 line:0%
IT'S NOT GOING TO WATCH
OUT FOR YA.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:44.843 line:0%
LET IT GO!

00:00:44.943 --> 00:00:48.080 line:0%
MARY MILLER: AH, HOLY (BLEEP),
I DON'T KNOW ABOUT THIS STUFF.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:52.652 line:0%
CURLY: MARY, YOU GOTTA
HAVE YOUR SAW FLAT.

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:55.555 line:0%
MARY MILLER: ALL I COULD
THINK OF IS THAT TREE

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:57.023 line:0%
IS COMING DOWN ON ME.

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:58.725 line:0%
CURLY, IT WANTS TO
GO THE OTHER WAY.

00:00:58.825 --> 00:00:59.893 line:0%
IT'S STARTING TO MOVE!

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:01.794 line:0%
CURLY: KEEP GOING,
MARY, DON'T STOP.

00:01:01.894 --> 00:01:04.230 line:0%
THAT TREE CAN BITE YOU
BACK IN A HEARTBEAT.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:07.333 line:0%
CUT FAST, CUT FAST,
KEEP GOING.

00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:09.368 line:0%
YOU MIGHT NOT LIVE TO
TELL THE STORY.

00:01:09.468 --> 00:01:12.772 line:0%
DON'T STOP, COME ON,
COME ON.

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:27.587 line:0%
MARY MILLER: I AM NOT READY
FOR WINTER AT ALL.

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:30.689 line:0%
THINGS GO IN THREES, AND WE
HAD THREE EASY WINTERS,

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:33.693 line:0%
SO I THINK THIS YEAR WE'RE
GONNA GET SLAMMED.

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:36.429 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: FOR THE PEOPLE
 OF SOUTHEAST ALASKA,</i>

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:38.564 line:0%
<i> THE KEYS TO THEIR FUTURE
 OFTEN LIE IN THE</i>

00:01:38.664 --> 00:01:42.068 line:0%
<i> LESSONS OF THEIR
 PIONEERING PAST.</i>

00:01:44.503 --> 00:01:46.705 line:0%
<i> FOR SEVEN YEAR RESIDENT,
 MARY MILLER,</i>

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:49.141 line:0%
<i> SURVIVING THE LONG ALASKAN
 WINTER REQUIRES</i>

00:01:49.241 --> 00:01:51.210 line:0%
<i> PLANNING FOR THE FUTURE.</i>

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:54.881 line:0%
<i> TODAY, THIS MEANS STOCKING
 UP ON FIREWOOD.</i>

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:57.283 line:0%
MARY MILLER: I'M NOT COMFORTABLE
WITH WHAT I HAVE HERE.

00:01:57.383 --> 00:02:00.786 line:0%
IT'S DEFINITELY NOT GONNA GET
ME THROUGH THE WINTER.

00:02:00.886 --> 00:02:03.222 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: TO GATHER A
 SUFFICIENT SUPPLY REQUIRES</i>

00:02:03.322 --> 00:02:06.092 line:0%
<i> MARY TO ADD A FUNDAMENTAL
 BUT PARTICULARLY RISKY</i>

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:09.295 line:0%
<i> SKILL TO HER ARSENAL
 OF TALENTS.</i>

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:12.364 line:0%
MARY MILLER: I PURCHASED A
NEW CHAINSAW THIS SUMMER

00:02:12.464 --> 00:02:14.933 line:0%
BUT I'VE ACTUALLY NEVER
CUT A TREE DOWN.

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:18.137 line:0%
AND, UH, I WANT TO BE
ABLE TO DO IT MYSELF.

00:02:18.237 --> 00:02:21.841 line:0%
OTHER THAN HAVE TO BARTER WITH
SOMEONE TO GET ME MY WOOD,

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:25.077 line:0%
I WANNA BE MORE
SELF-SUFFICIENT

00:02:25.177 --> 00:02:28.881 line:0%
BUT IT'S VERY DANGEROUS
FELLING TREES.

00:02:29.081 --> 00:02:30.916 line:0%
I GOT TO LEARN HOW TO
READ THE TREES AND

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:33.519 line:0%
WHICH WAY THEY'RE
GONNA FALL.

00:02:33.619 --> 00:02:35.888 line:0%
SO, I'VE NATURALLY
PICKED CURLY,

00:02:35.988 --> 00:02:40.259 line:0%
HE IS THE MAN WHEN IT COMES
TO FELLING TREES AND STUFF.

00:02:40.359 --> 00:02:42.294 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: KNOWN AS
 "THE WOODSMAN,"</i>

00:02:42.394 --> 00:02:44.830 line:0%
<i> 18-YEAR RESIDENT AND THIRD
 GENERATION LOGGER,</i>

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:46.766 line:0%
<i> TIMOTHY "CURLY" LEACH,</i>

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:48.701 line:0%
<i> HAS BEEN BEHIND THE
 SAW FOR 30-YEARS.</i>

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.870 line:0%
CURLY: MARY, SHE AIN'T AFRAID
TO GET HER HANDS DIRTY.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.405 line:0%
I MEAN, SHE AIN'T
SCARED OF BEARS,

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.573 line:0%
SHE AIN'T SCARED OF WOLVES,
SHE AIN'T SCARED OF THE

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:57.676 line:0%
SASQUATCH FOR CRYING
OUT LOUD.

00:02:57.776 --> 00:02:59.145 line:0%
MARY MILLER: WOAH,
YOU SCARED ME!

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:00.746 line:0%
CURLY: HA-HA, HEY, MARY!

00:03:00.846 --> 00:03:01.881 line:0%
MARY MILLER: HI.

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:03.649 line:0%
CURLY: SORRY, DIDN'T
MEAN TO SCARE YA.

00:03:03.749 --> 00:03:06.452 line:0%
THAT'S NOT TRUE THOUGH.

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:10.189 line:0%
YEAH, LOOKS LIKE YOU'RE
YELLOW-CEDAR PILE

00:03:10.289 --> 00:03:11.523 line:0%
IS GETTING DOWN THERE.

00:03:11.623 --> 00:03:15.527 line:0%
MARY MILLER: IT IS, I'VE BEEN
BURNING FAST AS I CAN CHIP IT.

00:03:15.627 --> 00:03:16.862 line:0%
CURLY: YEAH, RIGHT, RIGHT.

00:03:16.962 --> 00:03:18.964 line:0%
RIGHT NOW, PEOPLE ARE
COLLECTING THEIR

00:03:19.064 --> 00:03:21.300 line:0%
FIREWOOD AND THAT, THEY'RE
PRETTY HOT AND HEAVY,

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.502 line:0%
SO I'M GONNA TAKE MARY WITH
ME AND GIVE HER SOME

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:26.372 line:0%
POINTERS AND STEER HER IN
THE RIGHT DIRECTION.

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:28.774 line:0%
THAT'S A CUTE LITTLE SAW.

00:03:28.874 --> 00:03:31.010 line:0%
MARY MILLER: WELL, IT'S
A STEP UP FROM THE

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:32.678 line:0%
BARBIE SAW I WAS USING.

00:03:32.778 --> 00:03:35.247 line:0%
CURLY: YOU DON'T NEED ANYTHING
BIGGER THAN THAT ANYWAY.

00:03:35.347 --> 00:03:37.684 line:0%
MARY MILLER: I'VE JUST
CUT THESE ROUNDS ON

00:03:37.784 --> 00:03:40.085 line:0%
THE BEACH WITH IT IS
ALL I'VE DONE.

00:03:40.185 --> 00:03:41.420 line:0%
CURLY: UH-HUH.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:43.323 line:0%
MARY MILLER: I'M
A LITTLE LEERY.

00:03:43.423 --> 00:03:45.291 line:0%
YOU KNOW, YOU READ THE BOX
AND IT SAYS ALL THE DOS

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.593 line:0%
AND DON'TS AND THE CHAIN
KICKING BACK AT YA

00:03:47.693 --> 00:03:50.162 line:0%
AND THE BAR AND STUFF,
VERY FRIGHTENING.

00:03:50.262 --> 00:03:52.632 line:0%
MAYBE I WATCHED TOO MANY
SCARY B MOVIES

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:56.268 line:0%
WITH CHAINSAWS WHEN
I WANT TO.

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:57.737 line:0%
CURLY: LOAD UP.

00:03:57.837 --> 00:04:00.072 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: IN FACT, MARY'S
 ANXIETIES ARE WELL-FOUNDED.</i>

00:04:00.172 --> 00:04:03.643 line:0%
<i> AS PROFESSIONS GO, NONE
 IS DEADLIER THAN LOGGING.</i>

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:05.311 line:0%
MARY MILLER: THERE'S SNOW IN
THE FORECAST IN THE NEXT

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:10.416 line:0%
COUPLE DAYS, SO THIS IS MY
CHANCE TO GET OUT THERE.

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:13.052 line:0%
I NEED TO GO OUT THERE AND
LEARN THESE SKILLS AND

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:16.789 line:0%
GET IT RIGHT AND DO IT
NOW, OTHERWISE,

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:21.828 line:0%
IT'S GONNA BE A LONG
COLD WINTER.

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:30.435 line:0%
<i> [CHOPPING]</i>

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:32.505 line:0%
HANS PORTER: NATURE'S THE
MOST POWERFUL FORCE

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:34.940 line:0%
OUT HERE WE HAVE.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:37.043 line:0%
AND IF WE DON'T
MAINTAIN OUR TRAILS,

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:39.212 line:0%
MOTHER NATURE WILL
OVERTAKE IT AND

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:42.848 line:0%
YOU'LL NEVER FIND IT AGAIN.

00:04:43.682 --> 00:04:46.619 line:0%
TIMBI PORTER: I HATE
THIS ONE RIGHT HERE,

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:49.955 line:0%
THIS'LL BE SO NICE
TO GET THIS FIXED.

00:04:50.055 --> 00:04:52.124 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: HIGH ON THE HILL
 BEHIND THEIR PROPERTY,</i>

00:04:52.225 --> 00:04:54.593 line:0%
<i> 11-YEAR RESIDENTS,
 HANS AND TIMBI PORTER,</i>

00:04:54.693 --> 00:04:56.629 line:0%
<i> ARE FORTUNATE ENOUGH TO
 HAVE A MASSIVE SUPPLY</i>

00:04:56.729 --> 00:05:00.299 line:0%
<i> OF FIREWOOD THEY CALL
 "THE BLOWDOWN".</i>

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:01.934 line:0%
HANS PORTER: THERE WE GO.

00:05:02.034 --> 00:05:03.669 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: BUT KEEPING
 THIS RESERVE ACCESSIBLE</i>

00:05:03.769 --> 00:05:05.437 line:0%
<i> ALL YEAR ROUND WILL
 REQUIRE A SUBSTANTIAL</i>

00:05:05.537 --> 00:05:07.806 line:0%
<i> OVERHAUL TO THEIR TRAIL.</i>

00:05:07.906 --> 00:05:09.675 line:0%
HANS PORTER: AND EVERY
TIME WE GO UP THERE,

00:05:09.775 --> 00:05:12.011 line:0%
OUR TRAIL JUST KEEPS GETTING
WORSE AND WORSE.

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:16.582 line:0%
SO, WE'RE GONNA TRY AND
FIX THAT TODAY.

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:23.489 line:0%
TIMBI PORTER: THIS IS
RIDICULOUS, OH MY GOSH, HANS.

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:24.690 line:0%
HANS PORTER: YOU MADE IT.

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:27.559 line:0%
TIMBI PORTER: THE
THINGS I DO FOR YOU!

00:05:27.659 --> 00:05:30.529 line:0%
HANS PORTER: THANK YOU, BABY.

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:32.998 line:0%
TIMBI PORTER: BEING ABLE TO
GET UP TO THE BLOWDOWN IS,

00:05:33.098 --> 00:05:36.536 line:0%
LIKE, SUPREMELY IMPORTANT.

00:05:40.706 --> 00:05:43.009 line:0%
YOUR ACCESS BACK AND FORTH
TO YOUR WOOD SUPPLY

00:05:43.109 --> 00:05:44.910 line:0%
NEEDS TO BE SAFE.

00:05:45.011 --> 00:05:49.148 line:0%
WHEN YOU RUN OUT OF FIREWOOD,
IT'S SERIOUS.

00:05:49.848 --> 00:05:52.384 line:0%
HANS PORTER: WHAT I'M THINKING
IS, WE CAN TAKE THE ENDS

00:05:52.484 --> 00:05:55.921 line:0%
THAT I'VE CUT OFF AND THEN
PUT THEM IN THE MUD HOLE

00:05:56.021 --> 00:05:59.792 line:0%
AND SET PART OF THAT BEAM
RIGHT UP ON TOP OF IT.

00:05:59.892 --> 00:06:01.127 line:0%
USE IT FOR A BRIDGE.

00:06:01.227 --> 00:06:04.096 line:0%
TIMBI PORTER: I THINK THAT'S
PRETTY DAMN SMART.

00:06:04.196 --> 00:06:06.298 line:0%
HANS PORTER: FOR SOME OF US OUT
HERE IN PORT PROTECTION,

00:06:06.398 --> 00:06:09.001 line:0%
WHO'RE GETTING A
LITTLE BIT OLDER,

00:06:09.102 --> 00:06:11.304 line:0%
SEEMS LIKE OUR CHORES ARE
GETTING A LITTLE BIT

00:06:11.404 --> 00:06:13.038 line:0%
MORE AND MORE DIFFICULT.

00:06:13.138 --> 00:06:14.773 line:0%
TIMBI PORTER: IS THERE
A BOTTOM TO THAT?

00:06:14.873 --> 00:06:17.809 line:0%
HANS PORTER: ANY TIME YOU HAVE
TO GO THROUGH SHIN-DEEP

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:20.746 line:0%
MUCK TO GET TO
THE JOB SITE,

00:06:20.846 --> 00:06:23.949 line:0%
IT JUST KIND OF TAKES
A TOLL ON YA.

00:06:24.049 --> 00:06:30.322 line:0%
MAY SEEM LIKE A TRAIL TO YOU,
BUT, UH, FOR US ITS SURVIVAL.

00:06:30.589 --> 00:06:33.492 line:0%
TIMBI PORTER: HEY, THAT TURNED
OUT PRETTY WELL, LOOKIE, HEY.

00:06:33.593 --> 00:06:40.232 line:0%
HANS PORTER: 260 POUNDS,
SOLID, ALASKAN TESTED,

00:06:40.332 --> 00:06:42.801 line:0%
WIFE APPROVED.

00:06:42.901 --> 00:06:46.305 line:0%
THE STAIRWAY TO THE
MOUNTAINTOP NEXT.

00:06:46.405 --> 00:06:47.973 line:0%
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

00:06:48.073 --> 00:06:51.710 line:0%
TIMBI PORTER: I DON'T KNOW,
THIS IS GOING TO BE A PROJECT.

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:53.879 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: HAVING ONLY PUT A
 DENT INTO THEIR BATTLE WITH</i>

00:06:53.979 --> 00:06:56.415 line:0%
<i> MOTHER NATURE, THE PORTERS
 HAVE YET TO TACKLE THE</i>

00:06:56.515 --> 00:06:59.017 line:0%
<i> STEEPEST SECTION OF
 THEIR FIREWOOD TRAIL:</i>

00:06:59.117 --> 00:07:01.520 line:0%
<i> THE LENGTHY INCLINE
 TO THE BLOWDOWN.</i>

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:03.055 line:0%
HANS PORTER: THIS IS
WHERE IT'S BAD.

00:07:03.155 --> 00:07:04.824 line:0%
TIMBI PORTER: I KNOW,
EVERY STEP, MAN,

00:07:04.924 --> 00:07:07.426 line:0%
YOU NEVER KNOW IF THE GROUND'S
JUST GONNA GIVE WAY ON YOU

00:07:07.526 --> 00:07:09.462 line:0%
AND YOU'RE GONNA SLIP
IN THAT STUFF.

00:07:09.562 --> 00:07:11.430 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: IN A
 TEMPERATE RAINFOREST,</i>

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:14.099 line:0%
<i> THE FOREST FLOOR IS LARGELY
 COMPOSED OF THICK MOSSES</i>

00:07:14.199 --> 00:07:16.868 line:0%
<i> CARPETING CENTURIES OF
 DECOMPOSING DEADFALL,</i>

00:07:16.968 --> 00:07:22.274 line:0%
<i> RESULTING IN SOGGY, UNEVEN AND
 OFTEN TREACHEROUS TERRAIN.</i>

00:07:22.475 --> 00:07:24.276 line:0%
HANS PORTER: YOU KNOW WHAT,
MAYBE WE CAN GET

00:07:24.376 --> 00:07:25.845 line:0%
SOME STEPS PUT IN HERE.

00:07:25.945 --> 00:07:27.646 line:0%
TIMBI PORTER: IT LOOKS LIKE
WE'RE GONNA HAVE A HELL

00:07:27.747 --> 00:07:29.449 line:0%
OF A RUN OF STEPS
THOUGH, HUH?

00:07:29.549 --> 00:07:35.087 line:0%
HANS PORTER: WELL, IT'S ALL
UPHILL FROM HERE ON OUT.

00:07:40.892 --> 00:07:42.728 line:0%
GARY MUEHLBERGER:
OVER THE YEARS,

00:07:42.828 --> 00:07:45.297 line:0%
I'VE LEARNED THAT YOU GOT TO
TAKE CARE OF YOURSELF.

00:07:45.397 --> 00:07:47.733 line:0%
THE WINTER SEASON ALWAYS MAKES
EVERYTHING HARDER,

00:07:47.833 --> 00:07:49.702 line:0%
NO MATTER WHAT IT IS.

00:07:49.802 --> 00:07:51.737 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: SINCE PORT
 PROTECTION'S BEGINNING,</i>

00:07:51.837 --> 00:07:54.907 line:0%
<i> THE STAPLE RED MEAT HAS
 ALWAYS BEEN VENISON.</i>

00:07:55.007 --> 00:07:56.542 line:0%
GARY MUEHLBERGER: I'M A
LITTLE BIT BEHIND

00:07:56.642 --> 00:07:59.878 line:0%
IN MY HUNTING THIS YEAR, AND A
DOE THERE COULD BE CRUCIAL.

00:07:59.978 --> 00:08:01.647 line:0%
I'LL TELL YA, IT'S A LOT
OF WORK TO MAKE

00:08:01.747 --> 00:08:03.248 line:0%
IT THROUGH THE WINTER.

00:08:03.348 --> 00:08:05.451 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: HAVING HAD NO
 SUCCESS AT TWO HUNTS EARLIER</i>

00:08:05.551 --> 00:08:09.287 line:0%
<i> THIS SEASON, 70-YEAR-OLD GARY
 MUEHLBERGER IS CHANGING TACK</i>

00:08:09.387 --> 00:08:14.393 line:0%
<i> IN HIS FINAL EFFORT TO BAG A
 DEER BEFORE THE SNOW FALLS.</i>

00:08:16.695 --> 00:08:18.864 line:0%
GARY MUEHLBERGER: WELL, IT FROZE
PRETTY HARD LAST NIGHT;

00:08:18.964 --> 00:08:22.234 line:0%
IT LOOKS LIKE WINTER'S HERE.

00:08:22.334 --> 00:08:24.937 line:0%
THE BACKPACK'S FROZEN.

00:08:25.037 --> 00:08:27.940 line:0%
THE WEATHER MIGHT PUT KIND
OF A KIBOSH TO ME HERE,

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:30.409 line:0%
IT FROZE REALLY
HARD LAST NIGHT,

00:08:30.509 --> 00:08:33.245 line:0%
AND SO I'M GONNA HAVE TO MAYBE
GO IN THE TIMBER THERE,

00:08:33.345 --> 00:08:35.881 line:0%
THE MUSKEGS ARE
GONNA BE FROZEN,

00:08:35.981 --> 00:08:37.716 line:0%
EVERYWHERE I WALK IS
GONNA BE CRUNCHING,

00:08:37.816 --> 00:08:39.885 line:0%
I'M JUST GONNA BE TELLING
THEM THAT I'M COMING.

00:08:39.985 --> 00:08:42.254 line:0%
SO, I HAVE TO GET A DIFFERENT
APPROACH TO THIS,

00:08:42.354 --> 00:08:44.756 line:0%
AND I'M JUST GONNA HAVE TO
LOOK AND PLAY IT BY EAR.

00:08:44.856 --> 00:08:47.493 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: GARY PUTS 2.5
 NAUTICAL MILES BETWEEN</i>

00:08:47.593 --> 00:08:49.962 line:0%
<i> HIMSELF AND CIVILIZATION
 IN ORDER TO BETTER HIS</i>

00:08:50.062 --> 00:08:53.198 line:0%
<i> CHANCES OF A SUCCESSFUL
 DEER HUNT.</i>

00:08:53.298 --> 00:08:57.303 line:0%
GARY MUEHLBERGER: YOU CAN'T
GO TODAY, TRAPPER, SORRY.

00:09:07.346 --> 00:09:10.215 line:0%
MOST OF THE DEER ARE SHOT OFF
THAT SHOW THEIR FACE ON THE

00:09:10.315 --> 00:09:14.920 line:0%
ROAD SYSTEM THERE, THOSE ARE
THINNED OUT, THEY'RE GONE.

00:09:15.020 --> 00:09:17.857 line:0%
YOU HAVE TO GET WHERE THEY CAN'T
BE SEEN FROM THE ROAD,

00:09:17.957 --> 00:09:21.893 line:0%
YOU HAVE TO HUNT THOSE
PLACES OUT.

00:09:21.993 --> 00:09:24.096 line:0%
GETTING OLDER NOW AND
THOSE MILES ARE A

00:09:24.196 --> 00:09:27.399 line:0%
LITTLE HARDER FOR ME.

00:09:27.499 --> 00:09:31.904 line:0%
I GOT A 4-WHEELER THERE;
SOMETIMES I CALL IT A SCOOTER.

00:09:32.004 --> 00:09:34.273 line:0%
THE UNIQUE THING ABOUT
THE 4-WHEELER IS

00:09:34.373 --> 00:09:36.509 line:0%
THAT I CAN GET UP AND OFF
OF THE ROAD WHERE

00:09:36.609 --> 00:09:38.410 line:0%
I CAN'T GO WITH A TRUCK.

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:41.213 line:0%
OPENS UP NEW COUNTRY TO ME.

00:09:41.313 --> 00:09:44.650 line:0%
THE 4-WHEELER SOME PLACES CAN
DRIVE RIGHT UP TO THE DEER,

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:46.852 line:0%
I CAN WINCH IT UP,
THROW IT ON THERE,

00:09:46.952 --> 00:09:49.355 line:0%
AND I DON'T HAVE TO WORK
AS HARD TO GET IT.

00:09:49.455 --> 00:09:52.425 line:0%
WELL, HERE WE GO.

00:09:58.130 --> 00:10:00.499 line:0%
THERE'S A LOT OF COMPETITION
ON THE ROAD,

00:10:00.599 --> 00:10:02.702 line:0%
THERE'S A LOT OF YOUNG
GUYS THERE.

00:10:02.802 --> 00:10:05.270 line:0%
THEY COVER THE GROUND
PRETTY GOOD,

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:08.174 line:0%
SO I GOT TO GET OFF THE
BEATEN PATH TO SEE

00:10:08.274 --> 00:10:12.778 line:0%
WHERE THERE IS A DEER.

00:10:15.313 --> 00:10:17.383 line:0%
UH-OH, SOMETHING'S
THE MATTER HERE.

00:10:17.483 --> 00:10:20.686 line:0%
I MEAN, IT FEELS LIKE MAYBE THE
BELT'S SLIPPING OR SOMETHING.

00:10:29.161 --> 00:10:30.997 line:0%
GARY MUEHLBERGER: WHEN
YOU'RE GOING TO DO WHAT I

00:10:31.097 --> 00:10:33.299 line:0%
GOT IN MIND HERE, THERE'S A
FEW TOOLS THAT YOU NEED,

00:10:33.399 --> 00:10:35.134 line:0%
BUT IT'S JUST LIKE
A LOT OF STUFF,

00:10:35.234 --> 00:10:37.069 line:0%
THEY DON'T MAKE 'EM LIKE
THEY USED TO AND

00:10:37.169 --> 00:10:41.273 line:0%
YOU CAN'T RELY ON THEM
ALL THE TIME.

00:10:42.274 --> 00:10:47.346 line:0%
UH-OH, SOMETHING'S
THE MATTER HERE,

00:10:49.415 --> 00:10:51.249 line:0%
DOGGONE.

00:10:51.349 --> 00:10:53.218 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: MILES FROM
 PORT PROTECTION,</i>

00:10:53.318 --> 00:10:56.154 line:0%
<i> A MALFUNCTION IN GARY
 MUEHLBERGER'S ATV THREATENS</i>

00:10:56.254 --> 00:10:59.225 line:0%
<i> TO END HIS LATE SEASON DEER
 HUNT BEFORE IT'S EVEN BEGUN.</i>

00:10:59.325 --> 00:11:00.626 line:0%
GARY MUEHLBERGER: I
CAN FEEL SOMETHING.

00:11:00.726 --> 00:11:02.761 line:0%
IT FEELS LIKE MAYBE THE BELT'S
SLIPPING OR SOMETHING.

00:11:02.861 --> 00:11:06.632 line:0%
THE MOTOR'S TURNS UP AND
DON'T GO NOWHERE.

00:11:06.732 --> 00:11:11.036 line:0%
I'M THINKING THE OIL FROM
THE CRANKCASE IS GOING

00:11:11.136 --> 00:11:14.774 line:0%
INTO THAT OTHER CHAMBER.

00:11:15.941 --> 00:11:18.877 line:0%
SURE ENOUGH, THE
OIL'S DOWN.

00:11:18.977 --> 00:11:23.048 line:0%
SO, SOMEHOW THE ENGINE OIL
IS GOING INTO THE

00:11:23.148 --> 00:11:27.686 line:0%
CHAMBER WHERE THE BELT IS,
AND SO THE BELT IS SLIPPING.

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:29.621 line:0%
I KNOW FOR A FACT THAT
THIS ISN'T SOMETHING

00:11:29.721 --> 00:11:32.324 line:0%
I'M GOING TO FIX RIGHT HERE
OR ON THE ROAD HERE.

00:11:32.424 --> 00:11:38.430 line:0%
I'M JUST GONNA HAVE TO COME
UP WITH ANOTHER PLAN.

00:11:38.897 --> 00:11:42.968 line:0%
I GUESS I'LL JUST GO BACK
TO OLD SCHOOL.

00:11:43.068 --> 00:11:48.307 line:0%
GET MY RIFLE AND GO PUT 5
OR 10 MILES ON THE OLD FEET.

00:11:50.576 --> 00:11:55.648 line:0%
THAT'S THE WAY I USED TO
DO IT, HIT THE BRUSH.

00:12:00.586 --> 00:12:03.188 line:0%
AMANDA MAKAR: FINDING MY WAY
HERE IN PORT PROTECTION

00:12:03.288 --> 00:12:07.092 line:0%
HAS BEEN A LITTLE BIT
OF A CHALLENGE.

00:12:07.459 --> 00:12:10.829 line:0%
EVERYBODY HERE'S BEEN SO
HELPFUL AND I AM EXTREMELY

00:12:10.929 --> 00:12:15.333 line:0%
THANKFUL, IT'S MADE LIFE QUITE
A BIT EASIER HERE,

00:12:15.433 --> 00:12:18.536 line:0%
BUT I WOULDN'T HAVE
STAYED IF I DIDN'T

00:12:18.636 --> 00:12:21.240 line:0%
HAVE THE DETERMINATION TO.

00:12:21.340 --> 00:12:23.875 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: WITH THE OWNERS
 SOON RETURNING TO HER CABIN,</i>

00:12:23.975 --> 00:12:25.844 line:0%
<i> THREE YEAR RESIDENT,
 AMANDA MAKAR,</i>

00:12:25.944 --> 00:12:28.179 line:0%
<i> HAS ONLY THREE DAYS TO
 MOVE INTO HER HOUSEBOAT,</i>

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:30.849 line:0%
<i> THE WHY NOT, AND MAKE IT
 HER PERMANENT HOME</i>

00:12:30.949 --> 00:12:32.317 line:0%
<i> IN PORT PROTECTION.</i>

00:12:32.417 --> 00:12:34.653 line:0%
AMANDA MAKAR: I DON'T WANNA
FREEZE MY ASS OFF.

00:12:34.753 --> 00:12:36.488 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: BUT IN ORDER TO
 STAY WARM DURING THE</i>

00:12:36.588 --> 00:12:38.890 line:0%
<i> COLD NIGHTS ON THE WATER,
 AMANDA'S BEST BET FOR</i>

00:12:38.991 --> 00:12:42.961 line:0%
<i> SURVIVAL IS AN OLD-FASHIONED
 HEAT SOURCE.</i>

00:12:43.061 --> 00:12:46.999 line:0%
AMANDA MAKAR: THE WHY NOT HAS
ONE DIESEL STOVE ON IT,

00:12:47.099 --> 00:12:52.070 line:0%
BUT I GOTTA MAKE ROOM FOR A
WOOD STOVE BECAUSE

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:56.242 line:0%
MY DIESEL STOVE
ISN'T WORKING.

00:12:57.609 --> 00:13:01.046 line:0%
TRYING TO GET SOME OF THIS
STUFF OUT OF THE WAY.

00:13:01.146 --> 00:13:03.848 line:0%
PROBABLY ONE OF THE MOST
IMPORTANT THINGS TO FIGURE

00:13:03.949 --> 00:13:07.185 line:0%
OUT IN THE WINTERTIME;
KEEPING YOURSELF WARM.

00:13:07.285 --> 00:13:10.789 line:0%
WITHOUT HEAT, YOU'LL DIE.

00:13:10.889 --> 00:13:14.860 line:0%
OH, ANOTHER REASON WHY
YOU SHOULD OIL UP

00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:18.296 line:0%
YOUR RUSTY FASTENERS.

00:13:18.397 --> 00:13:24.303 line:0%
I JUST BUSTED THE TIP OF
MY SCREWDRIVER, SUCKY.

00:13:26.038 --> 00:13:28.506 line:0%
I CALLED ON MY FRIEND,
SAM CARLSON,

00:13:28.606 --> 00:13:30.876 line:0%
TO COME OVER AND HELP
ME PLAN OUT AND

00:13:30.976 --> 00:13:33.779 line:0%
INSTALL THE WOOD STOVE.

00:13:33.879 --> 00:13:35.647 line:0%
SAM CARLSON: YEAH, I WOULD
SAY YOU HAVE YOUR WORK

00:13:35.747 --> 00:13:38.417 line:0%
CUT OUT FOR YOU.

00:13:38.717 --> 00:13:41.253 line:0%
AMANDA MAKAR: AND THE SKY IS
BLUE AND THE GRASS IS GREEN.

00:13:41.353 --> 00:13:43.188 line:0%
SAM CARLSON: YEAH.

00:13:43.288 --> 00:13:46.725 line:0%
WHEN I STEPPED ONBOARD
AMANDA'S HOUSEBOAT,

00:13:46.825 --> 00:13:48.393 line:0%
IT KIND OF BROUGHT BACK
SOME MEMORIES,

00:13:48.493 --> 00:13:51.463 line:0%
BECAUSE I SPENT A WINTER IN ONE
WHEN I WAS IN JUNIOR HIGH,

00:13:51.563 --> 00:13:54.366 line:0%
AND I JUST REMEMBERED
HOW COLD IT WAS.

00:13:54.466 --> 00:13:56.034 line:0%
WOW, YEAH, YOU'RE GONNA
NEED SOME HEAT.

00:13:56.134 --> 00:13:57.369 line:0%
AND ONCE YOU HAVE HEAT,

00:13:57.469 --> 00:14:00.104 line:0%
YOU'LL HAVE A TOTALLY
DIFFERENT ATTITUDE CHANGE.

00:14:00.205 --> 00:14:01.606 line:0%
AMANDA MAKAR:
THAT'LL BE NICE.

00:14:01.706 --> 00:14:03.075 line:0%
SAM CARLSON: YOU'RE GONNA
WANT AT LEAST 12 INCHES

00:14:03.175 --> 00:14:05.978 line:0%
FROM YOUR WALL, JUST FOR FIRE
PROTECTION PURPOSES.

00:14:06.078 --> 00:14:08.981 line:0%
AMANDA MAKAR: MY BIGGEST
WORRY WITH THIS PROJECT

00:14:09.081 --> 00:14:11.684 line:0%
IS POSSIBLY BURNING
THE BOAT DOWN.

00:14:11.784 --> 00:14:14.586 line:0%
FIBERGLASS IS HIGHLY
FLAMMABLE AND

00:14:14.686 --> 00:14:18.791 line:0%
I'M GOING TO PUT A FIRE
SOURCE INSIDE THE BOAT.

00:14:18.891 --> 00:14:20.860 line:0%
SAM CARLSON: ONE OF THE INHERENT
DANGERS IN ACTUALLY

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:22.928 line:0%
HAVING A WOOD STOVE, ANYWHERE,
YOU WOULD DEFINITELY

00:14:23.028 --> 00:14:25.463 line:0%
HAVE TO HAVE ADEQUATE
FIRE PROTECTION.

00:14:25.563 --> 00:14:28.200 line:0%
THE MAIN THING IS SAFETY,
SAFETY FIRST.

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:31.537 line:0%
BOATS ARE KIND OF LIKE TRAILER
HOUSES, CONFINED SPACES,

00:14:31.637 --> 00:14:35.474 line:0%
YOU HAVE TO HAVE A LITTLE
EXTRA FIRE PROTECTION.

00:14:35.574 --> 00:14:38.644 line:0%
AMANDA MAKAR: I DO HAVE FAITH
IN SAM AND HIS CAPABILITIES.

00:14:38.744 --> 00:14:41.846 line:0%
I ATTEMPTED IT EARLIER
BUT I BROKE MY TIP

00:14:41.946 --> 00:14:43.282 line:0%
TRYING TO GET THIS.

00:14:43.382 --> 00:14:46.084 line:0%
SAM CARLSON: WHOOPS, I THOUGHT
MAYBE I COULD PULL IT OUT.

00:14:46.184 --> 00:14:47.619 line:0%
AMANDA MAKAR: LET'S
NOT DO THAT.

00:14:47.719 --> 00:14:49.888 line:0%
SAM CARLSON: IT FELT LIKE IT
WOULD JUST COME RIGHT OUT,

00:14:49.988 --> 00:14:51.823 line:0%
I DON'T KNOW WHAT IT'S
ATTACHED TO.

00:14:51.923 --> 00:14:53.359 line:0%
AMANDA MAKAR: THE WALL.

00:14:53.459 --> 00:14:56.762 line:0%
BUT WHEN YOU HAVE PEOPLE
COMING OVER AND JUST TEARING

00:14:56.862 --> 00:15:00.766 line:0%
PIECES OFF OF YOUR HOME IT CAN
BE RATHER CONCERNING.

00:15:00.866 --> 00:15:02.534 line:0%
SAM CARLSON: THIS IS GONNA GET
COVERED UP WITH DRYWALL SO

00:15:02.635 --> 00:15:05.838 line:0%
YOU'RE NOT GONNA
SEE ANY OF THIS.

00:15:06.238 --> 00:15:07.372 line:0%
JOB DONE.

00:15:07.472 --> 00:15:09.641 line:0%
AMANDA MAKAR: HANDLE REMOVED.

00:15:09.741 --> 00:15:11.410 line:0%
SAM CARLSON: UH-HMM, IT'S
A WEE BIT OF A CHALLENGE.

00:15:11.510 --> 00:15:13.645 line:0%
I'VE NEVER ACTUALLY INSTALLED
A STOVE, A WOOD STOVE,

00:15:13.746 --> 00:15:15.447 line:0%
IN A BOAT.

00:15:15.547 --> 00:15:19.919 line:0%
HOPEFULLY, WE WILL
BE SUCCESSFUL.

00:15:25.390 --> 00:15:27.559 line:0%
CURLY: TREE FELLING'S
A VERY DANGEROUS,

00:15:27.659 --> 00:15:30.796 line:0%
DANGEROUS OCCUPATION.

00:15:31.096 --> 00:15:33.398 line:0%
THAT TREE CAN BITE YOU BACK
IN A HEARTBEAT AND

00:15:33.498 --> 00:15:35.634 line:0%
YOU MIGHT NOT LIVE
TO TELL THE STORY.

00:15:35.934 --> 00:15:37.335 line:0%
ALL RIGHT.

00:15:37.436 --> 00:15:39.004 line:0%
MARY MILLER: THIS
IS THE SPOT?

00:15:39.104 --> 00:15:41.506 line:0%
CURLY: YEAH, THERE IS ONE
RIGHT UP HERE THAT

00:15:41.607 --> 00:15:43.775 line:0%
I HAD PICKED OUT
FOR YA THERE.

00:15:43.876 --> 00:15:46.311 line:0%
MARY MILLER: IT IS A LOT
OF CEDARS UP IN THERE.

00:15:46.411 --> 00:15:49.481 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: 2.5 NAUTICAL MILES
 EAST OF PORT PROTECTION,</i>

00:15:49.581 --> 00:15:51.816 line:0%
<i> SEASONED LOGGER,
 TIMOTHY "CURLY" LEACH,</i>

00:15:51.916 --> 00:15:54.052 line:0%
<i> HAS BROUGHT SEVEN YEAR
 RESIDENT MARY MILLER OUT ON</i>

00:15:54.152 --> 00:15:56.555 line:0%
<i> THE ROAD TO TEACH HER
 HOW TO CHOP DOWN A DEAD,</i>

00:15:56.655 --> 00:15:58.289 line:0%
<i> STANDING TREE.</i>

00:15:58.389 --> 00:16:00.259 line:0%
MARY MILLER: I THINK
I COULD HANDLE IT,

00:16:00.359 --> 00:16:03.728 line:0%
I WILL GIVE IT A SHOT.

00:16:03.828 --> 00:16:08.566 line:0%
I CARRY MY SAW LIKE CURLY
AND LOOK COOL NOW.

00:16:09.334 --> 00:16:12.137 line:0%
BEFORE I MOVED HERE I'VE
NEVER USED A CHAINSAW.

00:16:12.237 --> 00:16:14.773 line:0%
I COULDN'T EVEN LIFT THE MAUL
FOR SPLITTING ROUNDS,

00:16:14.873 --> 00:16:16.908 line:0%
BUT NOW I COULD SWING
IT ALL DAY LONG

00:16:17.008 --> 00:16:20.145 line:0%
AND SPLIT THAT WOOD
UP, YIKES.

00:16:20.245 --> 00:16:22.915 line:0%
CURLY: NICE EASY ONE THOUGH.

00:16:23.015 --> 00:16:25.717 line:0%
MARY MILLER: YEAH, EASY
FOR YOU TO SAY.

00:16:25.817 --> 00:16:27.886 line:0%
YOU KNOW WHAT THE HELL
YOU'RE DOING.

00:16:27.986 --> 00:16:30.255 line:0%
YOU JUST ACCLIMATE TO
WHAT YOU NEED TO DO

00:16:30.355 --> 00:16:32.291 line:0%
TO SURVIVE OUT HERE.

00:16:32.391 --> 00:16:35.360 line:0%
OH, I DON'T KNOW.

00:16:35.460 --> 00:16:38.063 line:0%
THIS IS SCARY, CURLY,
I CAN'T HELP IT.

00:16:38.163 --> 00:16:40.031 line:0%
CURLY: YEAH, I THINK SHE'S
PRETTY NERVOUS ABOUT IT.

00:16:40.131 --> 00:16:42.267 line:0%
SHE'S A LITTLE GUN-SHY
WITH THEM CHAINSAWS,

00:16:42.367 --> 00:16:43.902 line:0%
WHICH IS A GOOD THING.

00:16:44.002 --> 00:16:46.605 line:0%
MARY MILLER: I'M JUST GOING
TO GO, "AHH, I ALREADY KNOW."

00:16:46.705 --> 00:16:48.740 line:0%
CURLY: THEY SAY IF YOU'RE
NOT SCARED, YOU KNOW,

00:16:48.840 --> 00:16:50.742 line:0%
YOU AIN'T GOT NO BUSINESS
CUTTING TREES.

00:16:50.842 --> 00:16:53.378 line:0%
WHEN OPERATING A CHAINSAW,
YOU GOT TO REMEMBER THAT

00:16:53.478 --> 00:16:56.949 line:0%
SAW IS NOT YOUR FRIEND, IT'S
NOT GOING TO WATCH OUT FOR YA.

00:16:57.049 --> 00:16:59.384 line:0%
YOU'RE GOING TO CUT FLAT
INTO IT LIKE THAT.

00:16:59.484 --> 00:17:00.852 line:0%
MARY MILLER: GOOD LORD.

00:17:00.952 --> 00:17:02.154 line:0%
CURLY: YEAH.

00:17:02.254 --> 00:17:03.855 line:0%
MARY MILLER: OKAY.

00:17:03.955 --> 00:17:05.757 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: CHOPPING DOWN A
 TREE IS DANGEROUS BUSINESS.</i>

00:17:05.858 --> 00:17:07.759 line:0%
<i> AS SHE WORKS, MARY
 MUST KEEP AN EYE OUT FOR</i>

00:17:07.859 --> 00:17:10.128 line:0%
<i> FALLING LIMBS,
 KICKBACK FROM HER SAW,</i>

00:17:10.228 --> 00:17:11.930 line:0%
<i> AND LAST BUT NOT LEAST,</i>

00:17:12.031 --> 00:17:13.731 line:0%
<i> THE TREE ITSELF FALLING
 IN HER DIRECTION.</i>

00:17:13.831 --> 00:17:16.668 line:0%
MARY MILLER: BOY, I DON'T KNOW,
CURLY, IF I FEEL SAFE.

00:17:16.768 --> 00:17:19.471 line:0%
HOW AM I GOING TO LEAN OVER
THERE, GOING DOWNHILL,

00:17:19.571 --> 00:17:20.906 line:0%
WITH A CHAINSAW RUNNING?

00:17:21.006 --> 00:17:22.106 line:0%
YEAH, RIGHT!

00:17:22.206 --> 00:17:26.211 line:0%
CURLY: YOU CAN DO IT,
YOU'RE ALL RIGHT.

00:17:29.347 --> 00:17:30.916 line:0%
MARY MILLER: SMELL'S
FLOODED, I SMELL GAS.

00:17:31.016 --> 00:17:32.184 line:0%
CURLY: YOU SMELL GAS?

00:17:32.284 --> 00:17:33.651 line:0%
MARY MILLER: YEAH.

00:17:33.751 --> 00:17:34.852 line:0%
CURLY: RIGHT, HERE.

00:17:34.952 --> 00:17:36.354 line:0%
MARY MILLER: IT NEEDS YOU.

00:17:36.454 --> 00:17:41.593 line:0%
CURLY: THERE.

00:17:41.693 --> 00:17:44.997 line:0%
MARY MILLER: BOY,
I DON'T LIKE IT.

00:17:45.097 --> 00:17:49.168 line:0%
CURLY: I'LL COACH YOU THROUGH
IT THOUGH, GO AHEAD.

00:17:55.239 --> 00:17:57.709 line:0%
PUT DOWN YOUR HANDLEBARS
NOW, GET DOWN AND

00:17:57.809 --> 00:17:59.410 line:0%
JUST LET THE SAW GO.

00:17:59.510 --> 00:18:00.945 line:0%
IT'S KIND OF DIFFERENT
WATCHING SOMEBODY

00:18:01.045 --> 00:18:02.113 line:0%
ELSE CUTTING A TREE.

00:18:02.213 --> 00:18:05.016 line:0%
USUALLY, I'M ON
THE END OF THE SAW.

00:18:05.116 --> 00:18:08.487 line:0%
YOU WANT THAT POINTED,
RIGHT TO THE LEFT

00:18:08.587 --> 00:18:11.422 line:0%
OF THEM ALDERS, OKAY?

00:18:11.522 --> 00:18:16.161 line:0%
YOU'RE ALL RIGHT, YOU'RE DOING
JUST FINE, DON'T FREAK!

00:18:16.495 --> 00:18:18.463 line:0%
MARY MILLER: ALL I COULD
THINK OF IS THAT TREE IS

00:18:18.563 --> 00:18:20.298 line:0%
COMING DOWN ON ME, I'M GONNA
ROLL DOWN THE HILL, YOU KNOW?

00:18:20.398 --> 00:18:21.933 line:0%
ALL THESE THINGS THAT
COULD HAPPEN.

00:18:22.033 --> 00:18:26.004 line:0%
CURLY: THERE YOU GO,
TRY THAT, THERE YA GO!

00:18:27.005 --> 00:18:31.109 line:0%
MARY MILLER: AH, HOLY (BLEEP)
I DON'T KNOW ABOUT THIS STUFF!

00:18:31.943 --> 00:18:36.681 line:0%
CURLY: MARY, YOU GOT TO
HAVE YOUR SAW FLAT.

00:18:36.781 --> 00:18:38.483 line:0%
MARY MILLER:
AS OF RIGHT NOW,

00:18:38.583 --> 00:18:42.320 line:0%
I AM SCARED TO
DEATH OF THE THING.

00:18:42.420 --> 00:18:43.521 line:0%
CURLY: STOP.

00:18:43.622 --> 00:18:44.756 line:0%
MARY MILLER: OH, GOD,
CURLY.

00:18:44.856 --> 00:18:46.290 line:0%
CURLY: YOUR FINE, YOU'RE
DOING JUST FINE.

00:18:46.391 --> 00:18:48.359 line:0%
LET ME GET BACK OVER HERE
AND I'M GONNA WATCH.

00:18:48.459 --> 00:18:49.895 line:0%
MARY MILLER: CURLY, IT
WANTS TO GO THE OTHER WAY,

00:18:49.995 --> 00:18:51.096 line:0%
IT'S STARTING TO MOVE!

00:18:51.196 --> 00:18:56.735 line:0%
CURLY: YOU'RE FINE, DON'T PANIC,
JUST GO AHEAD AND CUT!

00:19:00.639 --> 00:19:04.943 line:0%
KEEP GOING,
MARY, DON'T STOP!

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:08.713 line:0%
CUT FAST, CUT FAST,
KEEP GOING,

00:19:08.813 --> 00:19:11.517 line:0%
DON'T STOP, COME ON!

00:19:21.159 --> 00:19:23.228 line:0%
MARY MILLER: CURLY, IT WANTS
TO GO THE OTHER WAY,

00:19:23.328 --> 00:19:24.595 line:0%
IT'S STARTING TO MOVE!

00:19:24.695 --> 00:19:26.864 line:0%
CURLY: DON'T PANIC, JUST
GO AHEAD AND CUT.

00:19:26.965 --> 00:19:28.700 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: OUT IN THE
 ALASKAN WILDERNESS,</i>

00:19:28.800 --> 00:19:30.568 line:0%
<i> FIRST- TIME LOGGER,
 MARY MILLER,</i>

00:19:30.669 --> 00:19:33.305 line:0%
<i> CONFRONTS HER FIRST
 DEAD-STANDING TREE.</i>

00:19:33.405 --> 00:19:38.177 line:0%
<i> AN INTIMIDATING
 90-FOOT YELLOW CEDAR.</i>

00:19:40.211 --> 00:19:44.416 line:0%
CURLY: KEEP GOING,
MARY, DON'T STOP...

00:19:48.286 --> 00:19:52.223 line:0%
CUT FAST, CUT FAST,
KEEP GOING.

00:19:52.323 --> 00:19:56.562 line:0%
CUT FAST, DON'T STOP,
COME ON...

00:20:06.804 --> 00:20:10.809 line:0%
GET OVER HERE.

00:20:11.043 --> 00:20:15.080 line:0%
SEE, YOU DID IT!

00:20:15.180 --> 00:20:18.216 line:0%
MARY MILLER: OH,
MAN, I DID IT, YAY!

00:20:18.316 --> 00:20:21.953 line:0%
CURLY: YOU DID IT, GOT AN
ADRENALINE RUSH GOING?

00:20:22.053 --> 00:20:24.322 line:0%
MARY MILLER: GOD, MY
HEART IS POUNDING.

00:20:24.422 --> 00:20:26.791 line:0%
CURLY: I BET.

00:20:26.891 --> 00:20:29.561 line:0%
