I FEEL PRETTY INTIMIDATED
BY MY WOOD STOVE.

00:30:04.168 --> 00:30:06.237 line:0%
I DON'T WANNA CATCH
ANYTHING ON FIRE,

00:30:06.337 --> 00:30:08.473 line:0%
BURN SOMEBODY ELSE'S
HOUSE DOWN,

00:30:08.573 --> 00:30:12.276 line:0%
OR PUT ANYBODY ELSE'S
LIVES IN JEOPARDY.

00:30:13.077 --> 00:30:16.914 line:0%
WHAT THIS DOES IS IT CREATES
A GAP BETWEEN THE WALL

00:30:17.014 --> 00:30:19.384 line:0%
AND THE SHEET ROCK
SO THAT THINGS HAVE A

00:30:19.484 --> 00:30:23.087 line:0%
CHANCE TO KEEP COOL, TA-DA!

00:30:23.187 --> 00:30:27.625 line:0%
SO NOTHING CATCHES ON FIRE.

00:30:32.129 --> 00:30:34.332 line:0%
SAM CARLSON: I'D SAY IT'S
ABOUT FACTORY PERFECT.

00:30:34.432 --> 00:30:37.402 line:0%
ALWAYS NICE WHEN A PLAN
COMES TOGETHER.

00:30:37.502 --> 00:30:39.170 line:0%
TAKE THIS OVER TO AMANDA'S
AND HOPEFULLY,

00:30:39.270 --> 00:30:43.575 line:0%
SHE'LL HAVE A HOT BOAT
BY TOMORROW.

00:30:54.251 --> 00:30:58.423 line:0%
AHOY, SPECIAL DELIVERY.

00:30:58.523 --> 00:30:59.757 line:0%
AND THERE YOU GO.

00:30:59.857 --> 00:31:00.891 line:0%
AMANDA MAKAR: GOT IT.

00:31:00.991 --> 00:31:02.159 line:0%
SAM CARLSON: GOT IT.

00:31:02.259 --> 00:31:04.562 line:0%
AMANDA MAKAR:
LOOKS GREAT, SAM!

00:31:04.662 --> 00:31:07.064 line:0%
SAM CARLSON: ALL RIGHT,
YEAH, THAT LOOKS GREAT.

00:31:07.164 --> 00:31:09.901 line:0%
AMANDA MAKAR: I HIRED THE
RIGHT MAN FOR THE JOB.

00:31:10.001 --> 00:31:11.736 line:0%
SAM CARLSON: AND THIS,
THEY'LL BE,

00:31:11.836 --> 00:31:15.106 line:0%
AND I'D LIKE TO SEE THAT AT
LEAST THAT FAR FROM THIS WALL.

00:31:15.206 --> 00:31:16.541 line:0%
AMANDA MAKAR: UH-HUH.

00:31:16.641 --> 00:31:22.080 line:0%
SAM CARLSON: OH (BLEEP)
SEE, WE'RE OFF.

00:31:29.921 --> 00:31:33.291 line:0%
SAM CARLSON: SPECIAL DELIVERY,
AND THERE YOU GO.

00:31:33.591 --> 00:31:34.758 line:0%
AMANDA MAKAR: GOT IT.

00:31:34.858 --> 00:31:36.093 line:0%
SAM CARLSON: GOT IT.

00:31:36.193 --> 00:31:37.661 line:0%
AMANDA MAKAR:
LOOKS GREAT, SAM!

00:31:37.761 --> 00:31:39.396 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: WITH THE NEW
 WOOD STOVE ASSEMBLED,</i>

00:31:39.496 --> 00:31:41.032 line:0%
<i> SAM RETURNS TO AMANDA'S
 HOUSEBOAT TO</i>

00:31:41.132 --> 00:31:42.566 line:0%
<i> COMPLETE THE INSTALLATION.</i>

00:31:42.666 --> 00:31:44.202 line:0%
SAM CARLSON: I'D LIKE TO
SEE THAT AT LEAST

00:31:44.302 --> 00:31:46.537 line:0%
THAT FAR FROM THIS WALL.

00:31:46.637 --> 00:31:48.206 line:0%
AMANDA MAKAR: UH-HUH.

00:31:48.306 --> 00:31:50.475 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: BUT HE DISCOVERS A
 GLARING ISSUE.</i>

00:31:50.575 --> 00:31:54.913 line:0%
SAM CARLSON: OH (BLEEP)
SEE, WE'RE OFF.

00:31:56.147 --> 00:31:58.683 line:0%
WE CAN'T USE THIS
AS THE MIDDLE.

00:31:58.783 --> 00:32:00.852 line:0%
STOVEPIPE'S ACTUALLY
GONNA BE OVER HERE.

00:32:00.952 --> 00:32:02.786 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: HAVING FAILED
 TO TAKE INTO ACCOUNT</i>

00:32:02.886 --> 00:32:04.755 line:0%
<i> THE PLACEMENT OF THE
 CEILING JOIST,</i>

00:32:04.856 --> 00:32:06.557 line:0%
<i> SAM AND AMANDA WILL NOW
 HAVE TO SHIFT THE</i>

00:32:06.658 --> 00:32:10.561 line:0%
<i> STOVES INSTALLATION ONE
 FOOT TO THE RIGHT.</i>

00:32:10.661 --> 00:32:12.597 line:0%
SAM CARLSON: I DON'T GENERALLY
DRAW UP PLANS OR SCHEMATICS.

00:32:12.697 --> 00:32:14.464 line:0%
I JUST HAVE THIS THING
IN MY HEAD.

00:32:14.565 --> 00:32:16.867 line:0%
GENERALLY, THERE'S ALWAYS
MODIFICATIONS ON THE

00:32:16.968 --> 00:32:18.435 line:0%
FLY WHILE YOU'RE
DOING THE JOB,

00:32:18.536 --> 00:32:21.806 line:0%
SO I JUST HOPE THERE'S NO
BIG STUMBLING BLOCK.

00:32:21.906 --> 00:32:25.109 line:0%
AMANDA MAKAR: GOD,
I HOPE THIS WORKS,

00:32:31.248 --> 00:32:33.751 line:0%
I CAN'T BELIEVE WE'RE
CUTTING A HOLE IN

00:32:33.851 --> 00:32:39.023 line:0%
MY PERFECTLY FINE ROOF.

00:32:40.858 --> 00:32:42.326 line:0%
SAM CARLSON: I HEAR AMANDA
DOWN BELOW GOING

00:32:42.426 --> 00:32:45.663 line:0%
"I CANNOT BELIEVE
SOMEBODY IS CUTTING A HOLE

00:32:45.763 --> 00:32:47.331 line:0%
IN THE ROOF OF THE BOAT."

00:32:47.432 --> 00:32:49.700 line:0%
YOU GO AHEAD
AND PUSH ON IT!

00:32:49.800 --> 00:32:51.101 line:0%
THERE YOU GO.

00:32:51.201 --> 00:32:52.469 line:0%
AMANDA MAKAR: SORRY!

00:32:52.569 --> 00:32:56.107 line:0%
SAM CARLSON: THAT'S IT,
DIDN'T GET ME.

00:32:59.210 --> 00:33:01.144 line:0%
THERE'S BEEN A
TREND IN ALASKA,

00:33:01.245 --> 00:33:02.880 line:0%
PEOPLE MOVING OUT OF THE
BUSH AND THEN, YOU KNOW,

00:33:02.980 --> 00:33:05.449 line:0%
BACK INTO THE CITIES
AND IT'S NICE TO SEE YOUNG

00:33:05.549 --> 00:33:07.418 line:0%
PEOPLE THAT ARE
HANGING IN THERE, TOUGH,

00:33:07.518 --> 00:33:10.054 line:0%
LEARNING HOW TO DO
EVERYTHING RIGHT.

00:33:10.154 --> 00:33:11.855 line:0%
I THINK THAT YOU'RE GOOD.

00:33:11.955 --> 00:33:13.224 line:0%
AMANDA MAKAR: OKAY.

00:33:13.324 --> 00:33:14.926 line:0%
SAM CARLSON: YEAH, I THINK
YOU'RE GOOD, THAT'S FINE.

00:33:15.026 --> 00:33:19.230 line:0%
AMANDA MAKAR: I CAME TO PORT
PROTECTION BECAUSE OF A BOY.

00:33:19.330 --> 00:33:23.934 line:0%
THAT RELATIONSHIP DID NOT WORK
OUT AND I DECIDED TO STAY.

00:33:24.034 --> 00:33:27.171 line:0%
THIS PLACE HAS
CAPTIVATED ME SO.

00:33:27.271 --> 00:33:29.807 line:0%
THERE'S SO MANY THINGS
THAT KEEP ME HERE.

00:33:29.907 --> 00:33:33.277 line:0%
THE ENERGY, THE PEOPLE,
THE LIFESTYLE,

00:33:33.377 --> 00:33:38.382 line:0%
AND I CAN'T SEE WANTING TO
LEAVE IT ANY TIME SOON.

00:33:38.482 --> 00:33:43.621 line:0%
SAM CARLSON: I THINK IT'S TIME
TO CHRISTEN THE STOVEPIPE.

00:33:48.392 --> 00:33:50.694 line:0%
GARY MUEHLBERGER: I'VE
HUNTED DEER FOR TWO WEEKS

00:33:50.795 --> 00:33:52.930 line:0%
AT A TIME WITHOUT
GETTING ONE.

00:33:53.030 --> 00:33:56.534 line:0%
<i> [MAKING DEER CALL]</i>

00:33:56.634 --> 00:33:59.102 line:0%
COMING HOME EMPTY HANDED.

00:33:59.202 --> 00:34:02.440 line:0%
<i> [MAKING DEER CALL]</i>

00:34:02.540 --> 00:34:04.475 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: HUNTER GARY
 MUEHLBERGER HAS HIKED FOUR</i>

00:34:04.575 --> 00:34:08.178 line:0%
<i> MILES INTO THE ALASKAN BUSH,
 DOWN CLOSED-OFF LOGGING ROADS,</i>

00:34:08.278 --> 00:34:12.783 line:0%
<i> IN HOPES OF FINALLY BAGGING A
 DEER FOR HIS WINTER STORE.</i>

00:34:12.883 --> 00:34:14.618 line:0%
GARY MUEHLBERGER: ALL YOU GOT
TO DO IS JUST MAKE A LITTLE

00:34:14.718 --> 00:34:16.854 line:0%
BIT OF NOISE AND THEM DEER
WILL EVADE YOU,

00:34:16.954 --> 00:34:18.956 line:0%
THEY CIRCLE AROUND BEHIND
YOU AND YOU NEVER

00:34:19.056 --> 00:34:22.793 line:0%
SEE THEM AGAIN, SO, WINTER
ISN'T WHAT GETS YOU,

00:34:22.893 --> 00:34:26.197 line:0%
IT'S NOT BEING PREPARED FOR
WINTER THAT'S WHAT'LL GET YOU.

00:34:26.297 --> 00:34:29.900 line:0%
I NEED A CERTAIN AMOUNT, IF I
DON'T CATCH ONE TODAY,

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:34.605 line:0%
THIS IS MY LAST CHANCE
FOR THIS YEAR.

00:34:34.705 --> 00:34:38.976 line:0%
I JUST KIND OF HAVE A LITTLE
FEELING FOR WHERE I AM

00:34:39.076 --> 00:34:41.345 line:0%
AND DIFFERENT DIRECTION.

00:34:41.445 --> 00:34:43.313 line:0%
I'M SWITCHING DIRECTIONS
ALL THE TIME,

00:34:43.413 --> 00:34:45.983 line:0%
BUT I'M JUST GOING BY
THE DEER TRAIL.

00:34:46.083 --> 00:34:48.685 line:0%
I DON'T KNOW HOW MANY MORE
YEARS I'LL BE ABLE TO THIS,

00:34:48.786 --> 00:34:50.654 line:0%
BUT I CAN GIVE THE YOUNG
GUYS A LITTLE RUN FOR

00:34:50.754 --> 00:34:55.159 line:0%
THEIR MONEY JUST BECAUSE
OF EXPERIENCE.

00:35:02.232 --> 00:35:06.570 line:0%
THEY MAKE IT TOUGH,
DON'T THEY?

00:35:06.870 --> 00:35:11.042 line:0%
BUT THERE'S DEER ALL OVER
IN THIS COUNTRY HERE.

00:35:11.842 --> 00:35:15.880 line:0%
THIS IS FRESH, IT
AIN'T FROZEN.

00:35:22.953 --> 00:35:24.488 line:0%
WELL, THERE'S DEER HERE.

00:35:24.589 --> 00:35:26.056 line:0%
THERE'S ALL KIND
OF SIGN THERE,

00:35:26.156 --> 00:35:27.424 line:0%
THEY'RE RUBBING ALL
OVER HERE.

00:35:27.524 --> 00:35:30.160 line:0%
THIS IS GOOD A SPOT AS ANY,
MAYBE BETTER THAN SOME.

00:35:30.260 --> 00:35:32.196 line:0%
YOU JUST HAVE TO
KEEP TRYING.

00:35:32.296 --> 00:35:34.832 line:0%
EVENTUALLY, ONE WILL
MAKE A MISTAKE

00:35:34.932 --> 00:35:38.769 line:0%
AND HOPEFULLY, I WON'T.

00:35:40.037 --> 00:35:42.940 line:0%
THEY'RE LIVING HERE,

00:35:43.040 --> 00:35:47.745 line:0%
SO, SOMETHING'S AHEAD
OF US RIGHT HERE.

00:35:47.845 --> 00:35:53.718 line:0%
IT'S PRETTY BRUSHY, BUT
THERE'S STILL A FEW OPEN SPOTS.

00:35:56.621 --> 00:35:58.723 line:0%
DID YOU SEE IT?

00:36:04.695 --> 00:36:06.830 line:0%
<i> [GUNSHOT]</i>

00:36:06.930 --> 00:36:10.501 line:0%
SHE'S RUNNING.

00:36:17.541 --> 00:36:19.176 line:0%
GARY MUEHLBERGER:
IT'S PRETTY BRUSHY,

00:36:19.276 --> 00:36:23.347 line:0%
BUT THERE'S STILL A
FEW OPEN SPOTS.

00:36:25.750 --> 00:36:27.818 line:0%
DID YOU SEE IT?

00:36:27.918 --> 00:36:30.287 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: AFTER THREE
 HOURS TRAVELING ON FOOT,</i>

00:36:30.387 --> 00:36:32.356 line:0%
<i> SEVENTY-YEAR-OLD GARY
 MEUHLBERGER FINALLY</i>

00:36:32.456 --> 00:36:35.626 line:0%
<i> HAS A DEER IN HIS SIGHTS.</i>

00:36:37.061 --> 00:36:39.230 line:0%
<i> [GUNSHOT]</i>

00:36:39.330 --> 00:36:43.000 line:0%
GARY MUEHLBERGER:
SHE'S RUNNING.

00:36:52.409 --> 00:36:55.513 line:0%
I'M GONNA PUT
HER DOWN THERE.

00:36:55.613 --> 00:36:58.783 line:0%
<i> [GUNSHOT]</i>

00:37:02.086 --> 00:37:07.691 line:0%
SHE'S DEAD,
IT'S A BIG DOE.

00:37:08.158 --> 00:37:12.163 line:0%
WASN'T A GOOD SHOT,
WENT DOWN.

00:37:12.363 --> 00:37:14.765 line:0%
THIS IS WHAT I WANTED,
THIS IS MY CHRISTMAS PRESENT

00:37:14.865 --> 00:37:20.137 line:0%
RIGHT HERE, SO THANK
YOU LORD, FOR THIS DEER.

00:37:23.707 --> 00:37:26.476 line:0%
THE OLD WAY IS THE
GOOD WAY FOR ME.

00:37:26.577 --> 00:37:28.812 line:0%
I'M IN PRETTY GOOD PHYSICAL
CONDITION BECAUSE

00:37:28.912 --> 00:37:31.215 line:0%
I WALK A LOT AND
WHAT I EAT.

00:37:31.315 --> 00:37:35.486 line:0%
I WAS REALLY SURPRISED
I COULD STILL RUN.

00:37:36.253 --> 00:37:39.423 line:0%
YOU WANNA DISPATCH THIS DEER
AS QUICK AS POSSIBLE.

00:37:39.523 --> 00:37:41.759 line:0%
THE BLOOD'S THE FIRST
THING TO SPOIL.

00:37:41.859 --> 00:37:43.526 line:0%
AND ONCE YOU GET THE
BACTERIA GOING,

00:37:43.627 --> 00:37:45.729 line:0%
THEN YOU DON'T
HAVE TOO LONG.

00:37:45.829 --> 00:37:47.865 line:0%
IF YOU CAN GET THEM
BLED OUT, GOOD.

00:37:47.965 --> 00:37:50.834 line:0%
YOU'LL HAVE SOME MEAT
THAT'LL LAST LONGER.

00:37:50.934 --> 00:37:52.369 line:0%
I GOT TO GET MOVING HERE.

00:37:52.469 --> 00:37:55.172 line:0%
IT'S GETTING DARKER AND I
GOT A WAYS TO WALK HERE

00:37:55.272 --> 00:37:59.610 line:0%
BEFORE I BE BACK TO
TRANSPORTATION.

00:37:59.710 --> 00:38:01.878 line:0%
WHEN YOU GET OUT IN
THE WOODS THERE,

00:38:01.979 --> 00:38:04.181 line:0%
OFF THE ROAD WAY OUT THERE,
YOU GOT TO FIGURE

00:38:04.281 --> 00:38:08.585 line:0%
OUT WHAT YOU'RE GONNA DO
ONCE YOU GET A DEER.

00:38:08.685 --> 00:38:11.922 line:0%
YEAH, BOY, I WISH I HAD THAT
FOUR-WHEELER RIGHT NOW BECAUSE

00:38:12.022 --> 00:38:15.492 line:0%
I COULD JUST PUT IT ON THE BACK
AND IT'D BE ALL DONE.

00:38:15.592 --> 00:38:18.629 line:0%
BUT IT'S BROKE DOWN AS IT IS,
I GOT TO MAKE A PACK OUT OF

00:38:18.729 --> 00:38:20.831 line:0%
THIS THING AND BE
THE MULE HERE.

00:38:20.931 --> 00:38:23.668 line:0%
GOOD THING MY NAME
IS MUEHLBERGER.

00:38:24.902 --> 00:38:26.904 line:0%
IN THE OLD DAYS, MY BROTHER
TAUGHT ME HOW TO MAKE A

00:38:27.004 --> 00:38:31.308 line:0%
BACKPACK OUT OF THIS DEER BY
TOGGLING THE FRONT LEGS.

00:38:31.408 --> 00:38:36.480 line:0%
I GOT THESE LEGS SKINNED OUT TO
MAKE A TOGGLE OUT OF THEM.

00:38:36.580 --> 00:38:40.751 line:0%
SO YOU TAKE IT LIKE THIS AND
YOU PUT YOUR FOOT THROUGH

00:38:40.851 --> 00:38:45.689 line:0%
THERE, PULL IT ON THROUGH, AND
THEN THERE'S YOUR TOGGLE.

00:38:45.789 --> 00:38:47.457 line:0%
THAT HOLDS THAT ONE.

00:38:47.557 --> 00:38:52.697 line:0%
YOU TAKE THE OTHER ONE,
SHOVE THE FOOT THROUGH,

00:38:52.797 --> 00:38:55.599 line:0%
TOGGLE IT OVER.

00:38:55.699 --> 00:38:59.402 line:0%
WELL, NOW YOU KNOW WHY I
WEAR A RED COAT BECAUSE

00:38:59.502 --> 00:39:01.872 line:0%
THIS ONE'S GOING TO TURN
RED PRETTY QUICK.

00:39:01.972 --> 00:39:03.841 line:0%
IT'S NOT THE EASIEST
THING TO DO.

00:39:03.941 --> 00:39:06.743 line:0%
BUT SINCE I DIDN'T HAVE MY
FOUR-WHEELER OR MY TRUCK,

00:39:06.844 --> 00:39:09.713 line:0%
THAT'S WHAT I'M GONNA DO
IS PACK IT ON MY BACK

00:39:09.813 --> 00:39:13.951 line:0%
THE OLD SCHOOL WAY.

00:39:18.322 --> 00:39:20.324 line:0%
I KIND OF PROVED SOMETHING TO
MYSELF TODAY.

00:39:20.424 --> 00:39:23.160 line:0%
I HAVEN'T DONE THIS
FOR A LONG TIME.

00:39:23.260 --> 00:39:25.963 line:0%
I COULD SHOOT A DEER,
PUT IT ON MY BACK,

00:39:26.063 --> 00:39:30.568 line:0%
GO THROUGH THE WOODS,
BRING IT BACK HOME.

00:39:32.936 --> 00:39:35.772 line:0%
I'M 70 YEARS OLD AND I STILL
COULD PUT THAT DEER

00:39:35.872 --> 00:39:40.044 line:0%
ON MY BACK AND PACK IT.

00:39:40.144 --> 00:39:42.780 line:0%
I LOOK IN THE MIRROR AND
THERE'S THIS OLD GUY THERE,

00:39:42.880 --> 00:39:49.086 line:0%
BUT I DON'T SEE ME THERE,
I'M STILL A YOUNG GUY.

00:39:56.360 --> 00:39:59.129 line:0%
MARY MILLER: THERE'S A LOT OF
THINGS THAT WE DO OUT HERE

00:39:59.229 --> 00:40:03.433 line:0%
TO SURVIVE AND MAKE OUR LIVES
MORE COMFORTABLE.

00:40:03.533 --> 00:40:06.470 line:0%
A LOT OF IT'S VERY DANGEROUS
AND YOU GET YOURSELF

00:40:06.570 --> 00:40:09.740 line:0%
IN SOME PRETTY SCARY
PREDICAMENT,

00:40:09.840 --> 00:40:12.109 line:0%
BUT YOU GOT TO LEARN BECAUSE
THAT'S THE ONLY WAY

00:40:12.209 --> 00:40:15.312 line:0%
YOU'RE GONNA NOT BE RELYING
ON OTHER PEOPLE.

00:40:15.412 --> 00:40:17.915 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: ON THE ROAD, CURLY
 AND MARY RETURN TO THE TREE</i>

00:40:18.015 --> 00:40:20.951 line:0%
<i> THEY FELL THE DAY BEFORE.</i>

00:40:21.051 --> 00:40:22.686 line:0%
MARY MILLER: WHY'S IT GOT
TO BE SO COLD?

00:40:22.786 --> 00:40:25.589 line:0%
IT MAKES EVERYTHING
TWICE AS EXHAUSTING.

00:40:25.689 --> 00:40:29.059 line:0%
YEAH, THE FORECAST CALLS FOR
THE SNOW TO BE FALLING

00:40:29.159 --> 00:40:32.196 line:0%
PRETTY HEAVY HERE COMING UP
THIS WHOLE NEXT WEEK,

00:40:32.296 --> 00:40:34.899 line:0%
SO IT'S REALLY IMPORTANT
TO GET SOME GOOD

00:40:34.999 --> 00:40:37.001 line:0%
HOT BURNING WOOD.

00:40:37.101 --> 00:40:39.136 line:0%
ME TOES IS FROZE.

00:40:39.236 --> 00:40:41.838 line:0%
CURLY: OKAY, YOU WANNA
FLIP THAT OVER MARY.

00:40:41.939 --> 00:40:43.974 line:0%
THERE YOU GO, YOU
GOT IT NOW.

00:40:44.074 --> 00:40:47.210 line:0%
MARY MILLER: SORRY, CURLY,
HAVING YOU HAVING TO BABYSIT.

00:40:47.310 --> 00:40:51.081 line:0%
CURLY: WELL, THAT'S ALL RIGHT,
YOU'LL, YOU GOT TO LEARN.

00:40:51.181 --> 00:40:53.117 line:0%
WHEN TEACHING MARY
HOW TO DO THIS,

00:40:53.217 --> 00:40:55.385 line:0%
I KIND OF FEEL A LITTLE BIT
RESPONSIBLE, YOU KNOW,

00:40:55.485 --> 00:40:57.854 line:0%
TAKING HER UNDER MY WING
AND THAT, YOU KNOW,

00:40:57.954 --> 00:41:00.024 line:0%
JUST PICK UP SOME GENERAL
POINTERS THAT

00:41:00.124 --> 00:41:02.092 line:0%
ARE GONNA KEEP HER
SAFE OUT THERE.

00:41:02.192 --> 00:41:03.494 line:0%
WELL, HERE WE GO.

00:41:03.594 --> 00:41:07.064 line:0%
MARY MILLER: OKAY,
LET'S DO IT.

00:41:14.805 --> 00:41:18.742 line:0%
GOD, YOU JUST MAKE IT
LOOK SO EASY, CURLY.

00:41:18.842 --> 00:41:21.645 line:0%
SOMEDAY, I WILL
BE THAT GOOD.

00:41:21.745 --> 00:41:23.947 line:0%
I'M FAIRLY LUCKY TO HAVE
A FRIEND LIKE CURLY.

00:41:24.047 --> 00:41:27.017 line:0%
IT'S JUST HUGE THAT PEOPLE
THAT HAVE BEEN HERE,

00:41:27.117 --> 00:41:30.553 line:0%
HOW MUCH THEY CAN HELP YOU
IN YOUR DAY-TO-DAY LIFE.

00:41:30.653 --> 00:41:34.991 line:0%
MAN, THIS THING WEIGHS
A TON, BEAUTIFUL.

00:41:35.558 --> 00:41:37.828 line:0%
CURLY: THE NUMBER ONE THING IS
IT'LL PROBABLY GIVE HER MORE

00:41:37.928 --> 00:41:39.996 line:0%
CONFIDENCE IN HERSELF
ABOUT GOING OUT AND

00:41:40.097 --> 00:41:44.201 line:0%
ACTUALLY DOING IT
ON HER OWN.

00:41:45.269 --> 00:41:49.840 line:0%
KEEP COMING, PERFECT!

00:41:50.741 --> 00:41:53.710 line:0%
MARY MILLER: OKAY, NOW,
DO I GO THIS WAY OR?

00:41:53.811 --> 00:41:55.512 line:0%
CURLY: GET IT IN
THE CUT FIRST.

00:41:55.612 --> 00:41:57.280 line:0%
MARY MILLER: BEFORE
